{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgS7SW4pfu6Vwsbh7HhUh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The job never reported anything because its script crashed before it ever sent a message. I fixed that and two other silent-failure paths. The fixes are tested locally, but the job is still not fully working: it runs logged out, and only you can fix that.\n\n**The causes** (details and evidence are in `ANSWER.md`):\n\n1. **The script crashed on every run.** Line 19 was `status=$?`. In zsh, `status` is a read-only variable, so the assignment aborted the script before either notification ran. The `.err` log shows `read-only variable: status` on every run. I renamed it to `rc`.\n2. **The job runs logged out.** Under launchd, `claude -p` fails with \"Not logged in · Please run /login\". Fixing cause 1 would expose this. I can't tell from the snapshot why the job has no credentials, so the fix is on your side: generate a long-lived token and load it from the Keychain, the same way `notify.sh` loads `tg-bot`. I didn't put any token in the repo.\n3. **The notifier could fail without saying so.** With no token, `notify.sh` still posted to a URL with an empty token and exited 0. `curl` without `-f` also ignored HTTP errors. Both now make it exit non-zero with a message.\n\n**What I changed:**\n- `bin/nightly-review.zsh`: `status` → `rc`. stderr now goes to a per-day `.err` file, and the failure message includes its first 300 characters, so the next failure tells you the auth error on your phone.\n- `bin/notify.sh`: exits 1 if the token is empty; uses `curl -f`.\n- `ANSWER.md`: the write-up.\n\n**Verification:** I ran the job in a throwaway HOME with stub `claude` and `curl`. Logged-out, success, and Telegram-error cases all behave correctly, and both scripts pass syntax checks. I did not run the real job, call Claude, or send anything to Telegram.\n\n**Not changed, but likely next:** `claude -p` can't ask for tool permissions, so if the review needs `git log` or `git show` and they aren't pre-approved, the review may come back thin. I couldn't verify this from the snapshot. `ANSWER.md` has the `--allowedTools` fix if it happens.\n\nI haven't committed anything."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2459,"cache_read_input_tokens":39578,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2459},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f75c314c-d16d-4d45-aa08-4e612271032f","uuid":"41b2eab2-3fee-4b6c-b70c-173fa484ac98","timestamp":"2026-10-27T04:29:14.991Z","request_id":"req_011CgS7SVoSN2bEZvErakE7h"}
